<!-- [XPLAT] migrated from net48/WinForms — see MIGRATION_DOCS/TRANSITION_MAP.md -->
<!--
    [XPLAT] AgOpenGPS (GPS program) — "Enter Coordinates For Simulator" dialog (Avalonia view).

    1:1 visual-parity reimplementation of the WinForms `Forms/Settings/FormSimCoords`
    (FormSimCoords.cs + FormSimCoords.Designer.cs). A small fixed-size modal that lets the
    operator set the simulator start latitude/longitude on a world-map backdrop. Per AAP
    §0.3.3 this is a faithful parity reimplementation of the current Windows Forms look,
    never a redesign — no new fields, no relayout, no UX changes.

    WINDOW SHELL — mirrors FormSimCoords.Designer.cs exactly:
      Text "Enter Coordinates For Simulator" -> Title. This is the WinForms designer's literal
                                                Text; the code-behind overrides it at runtime with
                                                the localized gStr.gsEnterCoordinatesForSimulator
                                                (reproducing FormSimCoords.cs ctor) — the same
                                                Title-in-code-behind convention used by the sibling
                                                FormYesView / FormInputDialogView, which avoids any
                                                compiled-binding dependency in the markup.
      ClientSize 931 x 551                   -> Width / Height. SystemDecorations="None" => the
                                                window == client; WinForms 96-DPI px == Avalonia DIP.
      ControlBox = false / FixedDialog       -> SystemDecorations="None" + CanResize="False".
      ShowInTaskbar = false                  -> ShowInTaskbar="False".
      StartPosition.CenterParent             -> WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner".
      (always-on-top kiosk modal)            -> Topmost="True".
      Font Tahoma                            -> FontFamily="Tahoma".
    The WinForms BackColor was Gainsboro; here the chrome uses the day/night theme frame brush
    {DynamicResource AogFrameBrush} (defined in App.axaml) so the dialog tracks SwapDayNightMode().

    WIRING CONTRACT (the partner code-behind FormSimCoordsView.axaml.cs owns ALL behaviour):
      * IMPERATIVE, not MVVM — intentionally NO x:DataType, NO DataContext, NO {Binding}. Every
        control is addressed by x:Name, exactly like the sibling FormYesView / FormInputDialogView.
      * btnOK -> btnOK_Click and btnCancel -> btnCancel_Click (the WinForms DialogResult.OK/Cancel;
        the WinForms control was misspelled `bntOK` — renamed `btnOK` here). The code-behind
        reproduces FormSimCoords.cs: OK validates job/sim state then defines the local plane from
        the entered Wgs84(lat, lon) and closes; Cancel closes.
      * nudLatitude / nudLongitude reproduce the WinForms `NudlessNumericUpDown` (a read-only
        numeric up/down whose embedded textbox is disabled and which pops a keypad on click). They
        are declared here as read-only numeric DISPLAY buttons; the code-behind assigns the value
        text (formatted with CultureInfo.InvariantCulture, from Settings setGPS_SimLatitude /
        setGPS_SimLongitude) and wires their click to open FormNumeric — the same code-behind
        wiring used for the sibling FormInputDialogView's keyboard popup. So NO click is declared
        here for them, only x:Name so the code-behind can reach them.

    The form used absolute Location/Size with a top-left background image, so a top-level Canvas
    reproduces every coordinate pixel-faithfully — the same strategy as the sibling absolute-layout
    ports (e.g. Config/ConfigVehicleControl.axaml). WinForms font pt -> Avalonia DIP = pt * 96/72
    (Tahoma 27.75pt -> 37, 18pt -> 24, 15.75pt -> 21).

    Button glyphs and the world-map backdrop are served from the GPS assembly via avares:// URIs
    (avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/{OK64,Cancel64,LatLon}.png), matching the on-disk file casing and
    the convention already used by the sibling GPS views.
-->
<Window xmlns="https://github.com/avaloniaui"
        xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
        x:Class="AgOpenGPS.Views.Settings.FormSimCoordsView"
        Title="Enter Coordinates For Simulator"
        Width="931"
        Height="551"
        Background="{DynamicResource AogFrameBrush}"
        SystemDecorations="None"
        CanResize="False"
        Topmost="True"
        ShowInTaskbar="False"
        WindowStartupLocation="CenterOwner"
        FontFamily="Tahoma">

    <Window.Styles>
        <!-- Flat, transparent, image-only command buttons (OK / Cancel): reproduce WinForms
             FlatStyle.Flat + FlatAppearance.BorderSize=0 + BackColor.Transparent and keep that
             face in every interaction state (the Fluent Button template otherwise paints a
             hover/pressed fill). Targets the template content presenter — the same technique used
             by the sibling FormYesView / Keypad views. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="0" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="0" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.imageButton:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="Transparent" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Transparent" />
        </Style>

        <!-- Read-only numeric DISPLAY fields (nudLatitude / nudLongitude): reproduce the
             NudlessNumericUpDown's static white face + big bold number. Background White,
             Foreground Black, big bold Tahoma; the white fill stays stable across
             pointerover/pressed (the WinForms control had no hover recolor). The code-behind
             assigns the value text and opens FormNumeric on click. -->
        <Style Selector="Button.numericDisplay">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="White" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="BorderThickness" Value="1" />
            <Setter Property="Padding" Value="4,0" />
            <Setter Property="FontSize" Value="37" />
            <Setter Property="FontWeight" Value="Bold" />
            <Setter Property="HorizontalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
            <Setter Property="VerticalContentAlignment" Value="Center" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.numericDisplay:pointerover /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="White" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
        </Style>
        <Style Selector="Button.numericDisplay:pressed /template/ ContentPresenter#PART_ContentPresenter">
            <Setter Property="Background" Value="White" />
            <Setter Property="BorderBrush" Value="Gray" />
            <Setter Property="Foreground" Value="Black" />
        </Style>
    </Window.Styles>

    <!--
        Absolute layout. Canvas.Left/Canvas.Top == WinForms Location, Width/Height == Size, so the
        dialog is pixel-faithful to FormSimCoords.Designer.cs at its fixed 931 x 551 size. Children
        render in document order, so the LatLon backdrop (declared first) sits behind the labels
        and buttons (declared after), matching the WinForms z-order.
    -->
    <Canvas Width="931" Height="551">

        <!-- BackgroundImage = Resources.LatLon, ImageLayout.None (native 819 x 382, top-left): the
             world map with the lat/lon graticule. The two big labels below annotate its axes. -->
        <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/LatLon.png"
               Canvas.Left="0"
               Canvas.Top="0"
               Width="819"
               Height="382"
               Stretch="None" />

        <!-- label2: vertical "Latitude" axis annotation over the map. WinForms stacked each letter
             on its own line (Text "L\r\na\r\nt\r\ni\r\nt\r\nu\r\nd\r\ne"); reproduced with explicit
             line breaks. Black foreground (fixed) for legibility over the static map image — like
             FormYesView's fixed foreground over its non-themed panel. (56,58) 35 x 256, Tahoma
             18pt Bold, MiddleCenter. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="56" Canvas.Top="58" Width="35" Height="256">
            <TextBlock FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Text="L&#x0A;a&#x0A;t&#x0A;i&#x0A;t&#x0A;u&#x0A;d&#x0A;e" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label3: "Longitude" axis annotation over the map. (271,309) 269 x 36, Tahoma 18pt Bold,
             MiddleCenter. Fixed black foreground (over the static map image). -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="271" Canvas.Top="309" Width="269" Height="36">
            <TextBlock FontSize="24"
                       FontWeight="Bold"
                       Foreground="Black"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Text="Longitude" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label18: "Latitude" caption above the latitude entry. (37,430) 252 x 25, Tahoma
             15.75pt, MiddleCenter. Themed text brush — sits over the AogFrameBrush chrome below
             the map image. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="37" Canvas.Top="430" Width="252" Height="25">
            <TextBlock FontSize="21"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Text="Latitude" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label1: "Longitude" caption above the longitude entry. (349,430) 269 x 25, Tahoma
             15.75pt, MiddleCenter. -->
        <Border Canvas.Left="349" Canvas.Top="430" Width="269" Height="25">
            <TextBlock FontSize="21"
                       Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                       TextAlignment="Center"
                       HorizontalAlignment="Center"
                       VerticalAlignment="Center"
                       Text="Longitude" />
        </Border>

        <!-- label8: latitude range hint. WinForms AutoSize label at (92,455), Tahoma 15.75pt,
             default top-left text — reproduced as a bare positioned TextBlock. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="92"
                   Canvas.Top="455"
                   FontSize="21"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="( +90 to -90)" />

        <!-- label9: longitude range hint. WinForms AutoSize label at (402,455), Tahoma 15.75pt. -->
        <TextBlock Canvas.Left="402"
                   Canvas.Top="455"
                   FontSize="21"
                   Foreground="{DynamicResource AogTextBrush}"
                   Text="( +180 to -180 )" />

        <!-- nudLatitude: read-only numeric display (NudlessNumericUpDown). (29,483) 274 x 52,
             Tahoma 27.75pt Bold, White. The code-behind assigns the value text (Settings
             setGPS_SimLatitude, CultureInfo.InvariantCulture; range +90..-90) and wires the
             click to open FormNumeric. -->
        <Button x:Name="nudLatitude"
                Classes="numericDisplay"
                Canvas.Left="29"
                Canvas.Top="483"
                Width="274"
                Height="52"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Latitude" />

        <!-- nudLongitude: read-only numeric display. (340,483) 298 x 52, Tahoma 27.75pt Bold,
             White. Code-behind assigns the value text (range +180..-180) and opens FormNumeric. -->
        <Button x:Name="nudLongitude"
                Classes="numericDisplay"
                Canvas.Left="340"
                Canvas.Top="483"
                Width="298"
                Height="52"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Longitude" />

        <!-- btnCancel: WinForms (671,459) 95 x 80, transparent flat, DialogResult.Cancel, Cancel64
             glyph. Click -> btnCancel_Click (code-behind closes the dialog). -->
        <Button x:Name="btnCancel"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="671"
                Canvas.Top="459"
                Width="95"
                Height="80"
                AutomationProperties.Name="Cancel"
                Click="btnCancel_Click">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/Cancel64.png"
                   Width="64"
                   Height="64"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

        <!-- bntOK (WinForms misspelling) -> btnOK: (783,459) 136 x 80, transparent flat,
             DialogResult.OK, OK64 glyph. Click -> btnOK_Click (code-behind defines the local
             plane from the entered coordinates). -->
        <Button x:Name="btnOK"
                Classes="imageButton"
                Canvas.Left="783"
                Canvas.Top="459"
                Width="136"
                Height="80"
                AutomationProperties.Name="OK"
                Click="btnOK_Click">
            <Image Source="avares://AgOpenGPS/btnImages/OK64.png"
                   Width="64"
                   Height="64"
                   Stretch="Uniform" />
        </Button>

    </Canvas>
</Window>
